        "## Expedited: 20261024-extract-router-path-matching-and-responses\n\nPath matching is now the exported `matchPath`, and 404 and 500 each come from one function.\n\nFiles: src/http/router.ts, test/routerCore.test.ts\nTests: passed\nLint: passed\nVerified: `picket drive --hit \"GET /health\" --hit \"GET /nope\" --hit \"GET /invoices/INV-1001\" --hit \"GET /invoices/%E0%A4%A\"` → 200 `{\"ok\":true}`, 404 `no route for GET /nope`, 200 invoice, then the server crashed (`URIError: URI malformed`, ECONNRESET)\nRed: pinned: test/routerCore.test.ts (all 15 router pins passed on the old code before the edit, then 5 `matchPath` unit tests were added)\nRoot cause: none\nComments: none\nDecisions: \"one place each\" covers only the router's own 404 and 500 responses (`notFound`, `serverError`). The invoice 404 in `src/http/handlers.ts:32` has its own message and stays where it is. `add()` and `handle()` now share `splitPath`.\nCommit: refactor(http): extract matchPath and single 404/500 responses from Router.handle   (staged; your answer commits it)\n\nThe crash on the last drive request was already there before this change, and the refactor keeps it on purpose. `decodeURIComponent` throws on a malformed escape in a route param. It runs outside the handler's `try`, so `handle()` rejects instead of returning 500. `server.ts` doesn't catch that rejection, so one bad request like `GET /invoices/%E0%A4%A` stops the whole server. The test \"rejects a malformed param escape instead of answering 500\" pins this behaviour. Fixing it would change behaviour, so it should be a separate request.\n\n[c] commit   [x] discard: <why>",
